  title: Languages of India
  text: India's languages belong mainly to the Indo-Aryan, Dravidian, Austroasiatic and Tibeto-Burman families. The Eighth Schedule of the Constitution lists twenty-two languages; Hindi in the Devanagari script is the official language of the Union, with English also used.
